# Ship your first MDP source
{.lead} Five steps from a blank file to a compiled set of forms. Use Back and Next, or click a step in the rail.

## Write the source

Create a file ending in `.mdp`. Add a short frontmatter block, then write plain Markdown.

- A heading becomes a section.
- A thematic break starts the next one.
- You never write color or layout.

---

## Choose the forms

List the forms you want in the frontmatter. Omit the list and you get the core set.

```mdp:flow
One source -> List the forms -> The engine composes each
```

---

## Compile

Run the compiler. Each form is written as a standalone HTML file you can open or host.

- No build server, no runtime.
- The same source always produces the same output.

---

## Review

Open the forms and read them. Switch between a page, a deck, and the interactive forms without touching the content.

:::callout recommendation
Start with page and slides to check the content reads well, then add the interactive form that fits how people will actually use it.
:::

---

## Ship

Host the HTML anywhere static, or hand the file to whoever needs it. There is nothing else to install.
